    <name>
      <text>Natural log improper Integral</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Calculate the integral \(\displaystyle \int_{{@lower_lmt@}}^{{@upper_lmt@}}{@func@}\,dx\)</p>
<p>\(\displaystyle \int_{{@lower_lmt@}}^{{@upper_lmt@}}{@func@}\,dx=\)[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]][[feedback:prt1]]</p>
<p>Therefore, the integral is [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p>Calculating the integral \(\displaystyle \int_{{@lower_lmt@}}^{{@upper_lmt@}}{@func@}\,dx\)</p>
<p>Using Integration by parts;</p>
<p>\(u={@expr_u@},du={@du@}\)</p>
<p>\(dv={@expr_dv@}dx, v={@expr_v@}\)</p>
<p>\(
\begin{align}
\displaystyle \int_{t}^{{@upper_lmt@}}{@func@}\,dx&={@part_uv@}-\displaystyle \int{@part_vdu@}\,dx\\
&={@int_parts@}\displaystyle|_{t}^{@upper_lmt@}\\
&=({@upper@})-({@lower@})\\
&=\lim_{t \to 0} \,\left[ {@upper@}-{@lower@} \right]\\
&={@upper@}-\displaystyle \lim_{t \to 0}\left( {@lower@} \right)\\
\end{align}
\)</p>
<p>Using L-hopitals rule \(\displaystyle \lim_{t \to 0}\, t^2 ln(t)=0\) </p>
<p>\(\displaystyle \int_{{@lower_lmt@}}^{{@upper_lmt@}}{@func@}\,dx={@ta1@}\)</p>
<p>Therefore, the integral is {@mcq_correct(ta_4)[1]@}</p>
<p></p>
<p></p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
